@startuml
title Manage Admin Account Sequence (/admin-accounts and /api/superadmin/admins)
autonumber
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
actor SuperAdmin
boundary "Admin Accounts UI" as AdminAccountsPage
control "AdminAccountsController\n(FE Dashboard)" as DashboardController
entity "AdminAccount\n(FE Response DTO)" as FeAdminAccountDto
entity "AdminAccountQueryRequest\n(BE Request DTO)" as AdminAccountQueryRequestDto
entity "CreateAdminAccountRequest\n(BE Request DTO)" as CreateAdminAccountRequestDto
entity "UpdateAdminAccountRequest\n(BE Request DTO)" as UpdateAdminAccountRequestDto
entity "AdminAccountResponse\n(BE Response DTO)" as AdminAccountResponseDto
control "SuperAdminAccountsController\n(BE API)" as ApiController
control "SuperAdminAccountService" as AccountService
control "ISuperAdminAccountService" as ISuperAdminAccountService
entity "User" as UserEntity
entity "UserAuth" as UserAuthEntity
entity "UserProfile" as UserProfileEntity
entity "Role" as RoleEntity
entity "RefreshToken" as RefreshTokenEntity
control "SuperAdminAccountRepository" as AccountRepository
control "ISuperAdminAccountRepository" as ISuperAdminAccountRepository
database "VocaNovaDbContext" as DbContext
database "MySQL Database" as MySQL
note over AdminAccountsPage, MySQL
Checked in current code:
Dashboard AdminAccountsController calls the API through VocaNovaApiClient.
API uses AdminAccountQueryRequest, CreateAdminAccountRequest, UpdateAdminAccountRequest, and AdminAccountResponse.
FE response DTO exists: AdminAccount for admin account list/detail data.
Lock/Unlock/Delete use route id only and return bool in the API envelope.
Interfaces used in code: ISuperAdminAccountService, ISuperAdminAccountRepository.
end note
SuperAdmin -> AdminAccountsPage: Open admin account management
AdminAccountsPage -> DashboardController: GET /admin-accounts(search, status, paging, sort)
DashboardController -> DashboardController: Normalize filter
DashboardController -> AdminAccountQueryRequestDto: VocaNovaApiClient.GetAdminAccountsAsync(filter)Create query data(page, limit, status,\nsearch, include_deleted, sort)
AdminAccountQueryRequestDto -> ApiController: GET /api/superadmin/adminsAdminAccountQueryRequest
ApiController -> ApiController: Check super admin authorization
ApiController -> ApiController: Validate AdminAccountQueryRequest
alt Request validation fails
ApiController --> DashboardController: HTTP 400 error
DashboardController --> AdminAccountsPage: Show error message
else Request validation success
ApiController -> ISuperAdminAccountService: GetAccountsAsync(query)
ISuperAdminAccountService -> AccountService: GetAccountsAsync(query)
AccountService -> ISuperAdminAccountRepository: GetAccountsAsync(query)
ISuperAdminAccountRepository -> AccountRepository: GetAccountsAsync(query)
AccountRepository -> DbContext: Query admin accounts
DbContext -> MySQL: SELECT users with admin role
MySQL --> DbContext: Admin account rows and total count
DbContext -> UserEntity: Materialize Users
DbContext -> UserAuthEntity: Materialize UserAuth rows
DbContext -> UserProfileEntity: Materialize UserProfile rows
DbContext -> RoleEntity: Materialize Role rows
UserEntity --> DbContext: Users
UserAuthEntity --> DbContext: UserAuth rows
UserProfileEntity --> DbContext: UserProfile rows
RoleEntity --> DbContext: Roles
DbContext --> AccountRepository: Result
AccountRepository --> AccountService: Paged admin accounts
AccountService --> ApiController: Return accounts result
ApiController -> AdminAccountResponseDto: Create response data(AdminAccountResponse)
AdminAccountResponseDto --> ApiController: Paged AdminAccountResponse
ApiController -> FeAdminAccountDto: HTTP 200 OK\nPaged AdminAccountResponse JSON
FeAdminAccountDto --> DashboardController: Paged AdminAccount
DashboardController --> AdminAccountsPage: Render admin account list
end
alt SuperAdmin creates admin account
SuperAdmin -> AdminAccountsPage: Submit create form
AdminAccountsPage -> DashboardController: POST /admin-accounts/create
DashboardController -> DashboardController: Validate form input
alt Form input invalid
DashboardController --> AdminAccountsPage: Show validation message
else Form input valid
DashboardController -> CreateAdminAccountRequestDto: VocaNovaApiClient.CreateAdminAccountAsync(input)\nCreate request data(full_name, email, phone,\npassword, status)
CreateAdminAccountRequestDto -> ApiController: POST /api/superadmin/admins\nCreateAdminAccountRequest
ApiController -> ApiController: Validate CreateAdminAccountRequest
alt Request validation fails
ApiController --> DashboardController: HTTP 400 error
DashboardController --> AdminAccountsPage: Show error message
else Request validation success
ApiController -> ISuperAdminAccountService: CreateAsync(create data)
ISuperAdminAccountService -> AccountService: CreateAsync(create data)
AccountService -> ISuperAdminAccountRepository: FindDuplicateAsync(phone, email)
ISuperAdminAccountRepository -> AccountRepository: FindDuplicateAsync(phone, email)
AccountRepository -> DbContext: Query duplicate phone/email
DbContext -> MySQL: SELECT user_auth
MySQL --> DbContext: Duplicate row or null
DbContext -> UserAuthEntity: Materialize UserAuth?
UserAuthEntity --> DbContext: UserAuth or null
DbContext --> AccountRepository: Result
AccountRepository --> AccountService: Duplicate message or null
alt Phone or email already exists
AccountService --> ApiController: Conflict result
ApiController --> DashboardController: HTTP 409 error
DashboardController --> AdminAccountsPage: Show error message
else Account can be created
AccountService -> ISuperAdminAccountRepository: GetAdminRoleIdAsync()
ISuperAdminAccountRepository -> AccountRepository: GetAdminRoleIdAsync()
AccountRepository -> DbContext: Query admin role
DbContext -> MySQL: SELECT roles
MySQL --> DbContext: Admin role row or null
DbContext -> RoleEntity: Materialize Role?
RoleEntity --> DbContext: Role or null
DbContext --> AccountRepository: Result
AccountRepository --> AccountService: role_id or null
alt Admin role missing
AccountService --> ApiController: Validation failure
ApiController --> DashboardController: HTTP 400 error
DashboardController --> AdminAccountsPage: Show error message
else Admin role exists
AccountService -> AccountService: Hash password and begin transaction
AccountService -> ISuperAdminAccountRepository: AddAccountAsync(create data)
ISuperAdminAccountRepository -> AccountRepository: AddAccountAsync(create data)
AccountRepository -> UserEntity: Create User
AccountRepository -> UserAuthEntity: Create UserAuth
AccountRepository -> UserProfileEntity: Create UserProfile
AccountRepository -> RoleEntity: Link Role to User
UserEntity --> AccountRepository: User
UserAuthEntity --> AccountRepository: UserAuth
UserProfileEntity --> AccountRepository: UserProfile
RoleEntity --> AccountRepository: Linked Role
AccountRepository -> DbContext: Add User, UserAuth, UserProfile
DbContext -> MySQL: INSERT admin account data
MySQL --> DbContext: Insert result
DbContext --> AccountRepository: Save result
AccountRepository --> AccountService: Created account
AccountService --> ApiController: Return created account
ApiController -> AdminAccountResponseDto: Create response data(AdminAccountResponse)
AdminAccountResponseDto --> DashboardController: HTTP 201 Created\nAdminAccountResponse
DashboardController --> AdminAccountsPage: Show success and refresh list
end
end
end
end
else SuperAdmin updates admin account
SuperAdmin -> AdminAccountsPage: Submit edit form
AdminAccountsPage -> DashboardController: POST /admin-accounts/{id}/edit
DashboardController -> DashboardController: Validate form input
alt Form input invalid
DashboardController --> AdminAccountsPage: Show validation message
else Form input valid
DashboardController -> UpdateAdminAccountRequestDto: VocaNovaApiClient.UpdateAdminAccountAsync(id, input)\nCreate request data(full_name, email, phone,\npassword?, status)
UpdateAdminAccountRequestDto -> ApiController: PUT /api/superadmin/admins/{id}UpdateAdminAccountRequest
ApiController -> ApiController: Validate UpdateAdminAccountRequest
alt Request validation fails
ApiController --> DashboardController: HTTP 400 error
DashboardController --> AdminAccountsPage: Show error message
else Request validation success
ApiController -> ISuperAdminAccountService: UpdateAsync(id, update data)
ISuperAdminAccountService -> AccountService: UpdateAsync(id, update data)
AccountService -> ISuperAdminAccountRepository: FindDuplicateAsync(phone, email, id)
ISuperAdminAccountRepository -> AccountRepository: FindDuplicateAsync(phone, email, id)
AccountRepository -> DbContext: Query duplicate phone/email
DbContext -> MySQL: SELECT user_auth
MySQL --> DbContext: Duplicate row or null
DbContext -> UserAuthEntity: Materialize UserAuth?
UserAuthEntity --> DbContext: UserAuth or null
DbContext --> AccountRepository: Result
AccountRepository --> AccountService: Duplicate message or null
alt Duplicate or account not found
AccountService --> ApiController: Conflict/NotFound result
ApiController --> DashboardController: HTTP 409/404 error
DashboardController --> AdminAccountsPage: Show error message
else Account can be updated
AccountService -> AccountService: Hash password if suppliedand begin transaction
AccountService -> ISuperAdminAccountRepository: UpdateAccountAsync(id, update data)
ISuperAdminAccountRepository -> AccountRepository: UpdateAccountAsync(id, update data)
AccountRepository -> UserEntity: Update status
AccountRepository -> UserAuthEntity: Update phone, email,\npassword_hash?
AccountRepository -> UserProfileEntity: Update full_name
UserEntity --> AccountRepository: User
UserAuthEntity --> AccountRepository: UserAuth
UserProfileEntity --> AccountRepository: UserProfile
AccountRepository -> DbContext: Track User, UserAuth, UserProfile
DbContext -> MySQL: UPDATE admin account data
MySQL --> DbContext: Update result
DbContext --> AccountRepository: Save result
AccountRepository --> AccountService: Updated account
AccountService --> ApiController: Return updated account
ApiController -> AdminAccountResponseDto: Create response data(AdminAccountResponse)
AdminAccountResponseDto --> DashboardController: HTTP 200 OK\nAdminAccountResponse
DashboardController --> AdminAccountsPage: Show success and refresh list
end
end
end
else SuperAdmin locks, unlocks, or deletes admin account
SuperAdmin -> AdminAccountsPage: Click Lock/Unlock/Delete
AdminAccountsPage -> DashboardController: POST /admin-accounts/{id}/lock\nor /unlock or /delete
DashboardController -> ApiController: VocaNovaApiClient.Lock/Unlock/DeleteAdminAccountAsync(id)\nPATCH /api/superadmin/admins/{id}/lock\nor /unlock\nor DELETE /api/superadmin/admins/{id}
ApiController -> ISuperAdminAccountService: LockAsync(id), UnlockAsync(id),or DeleteAsync(id)
ISuperAdminAccountService -> AccountService: LockAsync(id), UnlockAsync(id),or DeleteAsync(id)
AccountService -> ISuperAdminAccountRepository: GetAccountStatusAsync(id)
ISuperAdminAccountRepository -> AccountRepository: GetAccountStatusAsync(id)
AccountRepository -> DbContext: Query admin account status
DbContext -> MySQL: SELECT user status
MySQL --> DbContext: Status row or null
DbContext -> UserEntity: Materialize User?
UserEntity --> DbContext: User or null
DbContext --> AccountRepository: Result
AccountRepository --> AccountService: status or null
alt Account not found or already in target state
AccountService --> ApiController: NotFound/Conflict result
ApiController --> DashboardController: HTTP 404/409 error
DashboardController --> AdminAccountsPage: Show feedback
else Status can be changed
AccountService -> AccountService: Begin transaction
opt Lock or Delete
AccountService -> ISuperAdminAccountRepository: RevokeActiveRefreshTokensAsync(id)
ISuperAdminAccountRepository -> AccountRepository: RevokeActiveRefreshTokensAsync(id)
AccountRepository -> RefreshTokenEntity: Set RevokedAt
RefreshTokenEntity --> AccountRepository: RefreshToken updated
AccountRepository -> DbContext: Track refresh token updates
DbContext -> MySQL: UPDATE refresh_tokens
MySQL --> DbContext: Update result
end
AccountService -> ISuperAdminAccountRepository: ChangeStatusAsync(id, status)or DeleteAccountAsync(id)
ISuperAdminAccountRepository -> AccountRepository: ChangeStatusAsync(id, status)or DeleteAccountAsync(id)
AccountRepository -> UserEntity: Update status
AccountRepository -> UserAuthEntity: Clear auth fields if deleted
UserEntity --> AccountRepository: User updated
UserAuthEntity --> AccountRepository: UserAuth updated if deleted
AccountRepository -> DbContext: Track admin account
DbContext -> MySQL: UPDATE users/user_auth
MySQL --> DbContext: Update result
DbContext --> AccountRepository: Save result
AccountRepository --> AccountService: Saved
AccountService --> ApiController: Success result
ApiController --> DashboardController: HTTP 200 OK
DashboardController --> AdminAccountsPage: Show feedback and refresh list
end
end
@enduml
